# Curated for this embedded C++11 target (TI-Nspire, -fno-exceptions, -Os). This is deliberately not
# the full clang-tidy set. The families kept are the ones that catch real device faults rather than
# restyle working code:
#   bugprone and clang-analyzer   logic and memory errors, the class that reset the calculator
#   cert                          unchecked returns and unsafe calls
#   performance                   the copies and allocations that matter under -Os
#   portability                   surprises across the cross compile
#   concurrency                   a cheap guard even though the device is single threaded
#   misc-use-internal-linkage     file-local helpers that should not have external linkage
# The noisy style families (modernize, readability, most of misc and cppcoreguidelines) are left off
# on purpose, because this codebase has its own idioms and they would flag correct code by the
# hundred.
#
# Three checks inside the kept families are disabled because they only restyle code that is already
# correct: easily-swappable-parameters flags any two parameters of the same type, and the two
# string-find checks want every one-character search literal rewritten as a char.
#
# The runner (tools/tidy.sh) points this at the shipped algorithmic core and leaves out the two
# diagnostic-heavy device entry files. The resident-module _exit rule is a separate clang-query
# check, tools/resident-exit.query.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  concurrency-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -performance-faster-string-find,
  -performance-prefer-single-char-overloads
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: 'stepcas/src/'
